--Description: For the known U.S. patent “US-9166782-B2” (granted within 2015-2018), retrieve the 4-digit IPC codes of every patent it cites.  
--Step-wise logic:  
-- 1) Start from the focal patent’s “citation” array, flatten to obtain each cited publication number.  
-- 2) Join those cited publication numbers back to the PUBLICATIONS table.  
-- 3) Flatten each cited patent’s “ipc” array and truncate each IPC code to its first four characters (ipc4).  
-- 4) Return up to 20 records so we can verify that IPC information exists for the cited patents, a prerequisite for computing originality.
SELECT
    cp."publication_number"                              AS "cited_pub",
    SUBSTR(ip.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4)                AS "ipc4"
FROM
    PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS src
    , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => src."citation") cit
    JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS cp
         ON cp."publication_number" = cit.value:"publication_number"::STRING
    , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => cp."ipc") ip
WHERE
    src."publication_number" = 'US-9166782-B2'
LIMIT 20;
```
